  {
    "id": 65,
    "category": 2,
    "topic": "Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS) vs. Intrusion Prevention Systems (IPS)",
    "query": "What is the key functional distinction between the passive nature of IDS and the active nature of IPS?",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS) and Intrusion Prevention Systems (IPS) are critical tools for monitoring network traffic to identify and handle malicious activity.",
      "An IDS is primarily a passive monitoring tool. It inspects traffic and alerts security administrators when it detects suspicious patterns, but it does not actively block the traffic.",
      "Because it is passive, an IDS does not directly affect network performance or cause downtime if it fails. It is often used for compliance reporting and forensic analysis.",
      "An IPS, conversely, is an inline, active security device. It is placed directly in the flow of network traffic and has the authority to drop packets that match malicious signatures.",
      "The inline nature of the IPS means it can stop an attack in real-time. However, this also makes it a potential bottleneck for network speed and a single point of failure.",
      "Both systems often use signature-based detection, which compares traffic against a database of known threats. This is effective for known attacks but weak against new, custom ones.",
      "Anomaly-based detection is a more advanced feature found in many modern systems. It builds a profile of 'normal' traffic and triggers an alert when deviations occur.",
      "False positives are a major challenge for both systems. If a system is tuned too aggressively, legitimate traffic may be blocked or flagged, leading to operational disruption.",
      "Many organizations deploy both: an IDS for internal visibility to find threats that bypassed the perimeter, and an IPS at the edge to block incoming malicious traffic.",
      "Choosing between IDS and IPS requires balancing the need for active protection against the risks of network latency and the potential for disrupting legitimate business operations."
    ],
    "expected_indices": [
      1,
      3
    ]
  },
