      "Injection flaws, such as SQL injection, remain a top concern. These occur when untrusted data is sent to an interpreter as part of a command or query, altering the intended logic.",
      "Broken access control is another perennial issue. If web applications do not strictly enforce permission constraints, attackers can access unauthorized data or perform administrative functions.",
      "Cryptographic failures occur when sensitive data is transmitted or stored in cleartext. Protecting data at rest and in transit via encryption is a fundamental requirement.",
      "Secure coding practices require input validation and sanitization as a first line of defense. Never trusting user input prevents many common attack vectors.",
      "Principle of least privilege should be applied to the application code itself. Components should only have access to the resources and data necessary to perform their specific tasks.",
      "Automated testing, including static and dynamic analysis, helps developers identify these vulnerabilities early in the software development lifecycle (SDLC).",
      "Security headers, like Content Security Policy (CSP), can be implemented to mitigate risks such as Cross-Site Scripting (XSS), by restricting the sources of executable content.",
      "The OWASP Top 10 promotes a culture of 'security by design,' where security is considered at the architecture phase rather than added as an afterthought.",
      "Continuous learning and training are essential for development teams, as attackers constantly refine their techniques to exploit new vulnerabilities in modern application frameworks."
