      "The efficiency of solar cells has improved significantly over the last decade, making solar power one of the most cost-effective sources of energy globally.",
      "Wind energy utilizes the kinetic energy of air currents to turn turbines, which then drive generators to produce electrical power.",
      "Wind power is highly dependent on location, requiring areas with consistent, high-velocity winds. Offshore wind farms have become increasingly popular due to stronger, more stable winds at sea.",
      "Geothermal energy harnesses the heat generated from within the Earth\u2019s core. It provides a constant, base-load supply of energy, unlike the intermittent nature of solar and wind.",
      "While solar and wind are widely available, geothermal is limited to regions with specific tectonic characteristics, such as volcanic activity or geothermal hotspots.",
      "Integration of these technologies into the power grid requires improvements in energy storage, such as batteries, to manage the intermittent nature of solar and wind.",
      "Smart grid technology also plays a role, enabling real-time management of supply and demand to ensure grid stability with high renewable penetration.",
