      "Sudden changes in color or lighting can signal a shift in character state or represent a change in reality, such as a flashback or a psychological break.",
      "These visual elements work subconsciously, priming the audience to feel a certain way before the narrative explicitly explains the situation.",
      "Master cinematographers carefully calibrate these tools to ensure the visual style supports the thematic goals of the director.",
      "When lighting and color are used effectively, they become an invisible language, guiding the audience's emotional experience throughout the film."
